  "title": "Fed foragers go back out instead of resting at home",
  "question": "On the right, do the ants read as foragers who keep making trips to the food, rather than a colony that goes home and stays there once fed? Would you want this in the game, given the lab box result below?",
  "context_md": "Where this sits: scouting (shipped) gets ants to the food the first time; this is about the trips after that -- foragers earning extra for the colony, not just themselves.\n\nTest switch only (`PIXEL_PHYSICS_FORAGE_DRIVE=always`); nothing in the game changed.\n\nColony test bed, seed 22 (typical on every count), frames 6,000 to 18,000, one frame every 300. Magenta = empty ant, cyan = carrying food, red block = the food, nest on the left.\n\n**Left, today:** after a trip, a forager comes home *hungry* (a median 138 J, under its 200 J grant), eats back up off the nest floor, and then stays home until it is hungry again. Everything that sends an ant out reads its own hunger, so a fed ant never goes. Only 47 of 159 repeat trips began with the ant fed.\n\n**Right, the drive:** a forager that has been to the food once goes back out while fed -- it scouts and paces like a hungry one. 197 repeat trips began fed, and they walk out 3x faster.\n\nOver 24 seeds at 90 cells: trips per forager 1.46 -> 2.15 (more on every seed), food into the nest 2.3x, 45 fewer ants starve, and 72 ants are born against 10 -- the surplus goes into foragers' bodies and they bud. At 140 cells: trips 1.57 -> 1.97, food into the nest +59%, births 7 -> 48, starvation unchanged (those die before frame 4,000, before any forager exists).\n\n**The catch is the lab box.** There the food is plants that regrow, not a pile that refills. Ants move 53% more and carry 52% more home, but eat no more, breed no more (530 -> 470 births, median), and on 2 of 12 seeds the colony boomed early, grazed the box bare and died out (none on today's game). Versions that follow the colony's need instead did worse in both games. Reading the colony's hunger does almost nothing on the bed (the colony is fed once the early deaths are over) and killed 4 of 12 lab colonies at founding. Reading the food stored at home is a weaker version of this on the bed and ends lab colonies smaller.\n\nSo my reading: this is right where the food supply outruns the foragers, and it needs an off-switch where the foragers outrun the food. Real harvester ants have one: they stop going out when returning foragers stop bringing food.",
